{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels","id":1101798,"title":"Granting Incepts & Creating False Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-08T17:11:45-07:00","id":1101798,"title":"Granting Incepts & Creating False Angels","content":"What Arcana should be required to grant an ephemeral being an Incept?<br /> <br /> What about creating an Angel-like being that isn't bound to the will of the Machine? Creating an actual Angel would be off the table, since I assume the disconnect would immediately cause a Fall or at least render the being an Exile, and template creation is forbidden, but creating a facsimile seems like it should be doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:21:34-07:00","id":1101801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels#post1101798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Arcana should be required to grant an ephemeral being an Incept?<br /> <br /> What about creating an Angel-like being that isn't bound to the will of the Machine? Creating an actual Angel would be off the table, since I assume the disconnect would immediately cause a Fall or at least render the being an Exile, and template creation is forbidden, but creating a facsimile seems like it should be doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>An actual incept? Nothing barring Imperial magic. Spirits &quot;Shape Spirit&quot; spell might be able to get something close, you'd have to spend potency on shifting bane/bans, numina (even making your own which i think is probably imperial spell territory) etc etc. What you would end up is is still just a normal spirit with the trappings/special effects that make it appear like a angel though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:44:36-07:00","id":1101812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels#post1101798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Arcana should be required to grant an ephemeral being an Incept?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incepts are the result of angels tapping into fuller access to the God-Machine's infrastructural reality lattice. So, uh... go build your own God-Machine and hook your spirits up to that. Not technically impossible, but beyond the scope of casting a single spell, and probably much less efficient than improvising some Perfecting or Patterning Spirit buffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T17:51:22-07:00","id":1101815,"title":"","content":"This should be considered homebrew, so for the purposes of discussion let's exclude:<br /> <br /> 1) Not Possible<br /> 2) Requires Archmastery (unless you have a solid reason it would rely on one of the Imperial Practices as described in IM)<br /> <br /> I like the hooking into Infrastructure point, though.<br /> How might one accomplish hooking into either suborned or 'normal' Infrastructure via Arcana to grant an Incept? I don't believe there's any reason to assume that doing so would provoke an unwinnable CoW the same way that trying to override an Angel's programming would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T19:10:51-07:00","id":1101831,"title":"","content":"Hm. I could see maybe some kind of patterning effect that was required to connect an entity into an infrastructure. However, I would argue that - while not impossible - the effect you were going for would be unreliable at best. Now, it doesn't require Archmastery - but should the infrastructure in question be designed in some way against such connections - or should the God Machine notice and dislike this concept - then it would automatically fail simply because the clashes on the opposing entity are an autoloss. And the effects might be very unpredictable.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is to say it sounds like it could be an interesting way to tell a story. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:25:22-07:00","id":1101893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101831#post1101831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I could see maybe some kind of patterning effect that was required to connect an entity into an infrastructure. However, I would argue that - while not impossible - the effect you were going for would be unreliable at best. Now, it doesn't require Archmastery - but should the infrastructure in question be designed in some way against such connections - or should the God Machine notice and dislike this concept - then it would automatically fail simply because the clashes on the opposing entity are an autoloss. And the effects might be very unpredictable.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is to say it sounds like it could be an interesting way to tell a story. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Unstable Incepts...sounds like fun to me. What might be the consequences of using such a power?<br /> <br /> Besides GM attention, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T03:07:29-07:00","id":1101902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101815#post1101815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should be considered homebrew, so for the purposes of discussion let's exclude:<br /> <br /> 1) Not Possible<br /> 2) Requires Archmastery (unless you have a solid reason it would rely on one of the Imperial Practices as described in IM)<br /> <br /> I like the hooking into Infrastructure point, though.<br /> How might one accomplish hooking into either suborned or 'normal' Infrastructure via Arcana to grant an Incept? I don't believe there's any reason to assume that doing so would provoke an unwinnable CoW the same way that trying to override an Angel's programming would.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, individual Infrastructure doesn't seem to grant Incepts (if it did, Demon's could regain them with some hacking), so you'd have to do more than just suborn 1 Infrastructure. Considering the security protocols/oversight even Angels using Incepts has, I doubt you could just give your creations &quot;authorization&quot; either. Additionally, even attempting to do so would require knowledge of the G-M's workings that Mages don't typically possess. Maybe one who had it as an Obsession, and worked extensively with Unchained or Demon-Blooded might get close. Oh, and Incepts seem to be a core part of Angel design (in that the G-M would outright remove them if It could, unless needed).<br /> <br /> Summary: Archmastery is probably easier, if not (very likely) required.<br /> <br /> Now, maybe the Mage could make a <i>deal</i> with the God-Machine for limited access to Incepts for the Mage's creations. That still isn't the Mage granting them Incepts, but it is about as close as you can get.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to make your <i>own</i> &quot;Incepts&quot;? Look at what they provide and conceptually represent. How can your Mage go about mastering a facet of reality like that? Even being <i>able</i> to do so is more suited to the subject of a Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Or you could play with the Abyss. I'm sure some shard in it has what you need. And it's not like anything bad ever really happened from doing something like that, right...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-09-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T03:23:15-07:00","id":1101907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101902#post1101902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, maybe the Mage could make a <i>deal</i> with the God-Machine for limited access to Incepts for the Mage's creations.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101902#post1101902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could play with the Abyss. I'm sure some shard in it has what you need. And it's not like anything bad ever really happened from doing something like that, right...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these ideas have a lot of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:20:48-07:00","id":1102087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101831#post1101831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. I could see maybe some kind of patterning effect that was required to connect an entity into an infrastructure. However, I would argue that - while not impossible - the effect you were going for would be unreliable at best. Now, it doesn't require Archmastery - but should the infrastructure in question be designed in some way against such connections - or should the God Machine notice and dislike this concept - then it would automatically fail simply because the clashes on the opposing entity are an autoloss. And the effects might be very unpredictable.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich is to say it sounds like it could be an interesting way to tell a story. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably give a lasting condition to the spirit subjected to something like that, like he was &quot;infected&quot; by the god machine or harmed by his &quot;antivirus&quot; and &quot;firewall&quot;. or whatever is equivalent. <br /> <br /> Not a good way to get some good will in a spirit court, that. I would probably require a rather high gnosis and both Prime and Spirit as arcana for the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:35:53-07:00","id":1102092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1101893#post1101893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unstable Incepts...sounds like fun to me. What might be the consequences of using such a power?<br /> <br /> Besides GM attention, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHonestly... I would probably make the consequences very shot-in-the-dark. You connect someone, but if you don't fully understand the infrastructure (and sometimes even when you do!) you can't really prepare for the results of such a connection. The 'effect' I have in mind is less 'you are casting a spell granting incepts' and more 'you are arranging circumstances that cause an entity to get incepts'. It is not as controlled.<br /> <br /> \u200bLokiel suggested a good result - your entities could very well become infected, and what was once an ally under your control might become a pawn of something else. Can you imagine, a spirit suddenly being given an angel's directive? What it that directive contrasted with the nature of the spirit? The results could almost be like a parallel to magath - or much worse, depending on your STs imagination","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:55:15-07:00","id":1102099,"title":"","content":"As far as making your own Angels, that might be quite a bit easier, though. Dave Brookshaw has stated Angels can be dealt with with Prime + Spirit, so a Prime/Spirit Making Spell should be able to construct somethng resembling an Angel and on their &quot;wavelength&quot;, even if it isn't strictly an Angel. If you wanted to jack it into some suborned Infrastructure, you might even be able to support more than one of them...but if you wanted to exapnd, you'd need to suborn more Infrastructure, or build it yourself, and eventually you might start playing around with replacing a bit of yourself with it and then one thing leads to another, and oops, you are and always have been the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:18:33-07:00","id":1102106,"title":"","content":"Related - do we know what phase of Twilight Angels are in, as it relates to Arcana?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:01:34-07:00","id":1102120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102092#post1102092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHonestly... I would probably make the consequences very shot-in-the-dark. You connect someone, but if you don't fully understand the infrastructure (and sometimes even when you do!) you can't really prepare for the results of such a connection. The 'effect' I have in mind is less 'you are casting a spell granting incepts' and more 'you are arranging circumstances that cause an entity to get incepts'. It is not as controlled.<br /> <br /> \u200bLokiel suggested a good result - your entities could very well become infected, and what was once an ally under your control might become a pawn of something else. Can you imagine, a spirit suddenly being given an angel's directive? What it that directive contrasted with the nature of the spirit? The results could almost be like a parallel to magath - or much worse, depending on your STs imagination</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say, a clever storyteller could use that to foreshadow a bit about what he envisions as being the true nature of angels: are they spirits transformed by the god machine? Are they something else? It could even be gradual and make for a good mystery. <br /> <br /> Malonkey said that you could make angels with prime and spirit. I think you could make something that, at a passing glance, look like an angel but wouldn't have much of its powers: no cover, no incepts, no futuristic biotechnology, ... All those are way too tied into the God Machine itself. And here's a question: shouldn't an artificial angel built without a connection to the God Machine fall at the moment of its creation? But what would a demon who fell so suddendly and without any prior contact with the God Machine and humanity be like, what would be its identity and sense of self? Especially since he wouldn't have a &quot;starting cover&quot;. Furthermore, without any prior contact with the god machine, could he use all of the powers of its fellow demons? Several of them are described as a demon &quot;remembering&quot; the powers the god machine gave to its angels and twisting them into something usable. (For instance, I believe exploits are described like that). And if because of all this it doesn't fall instantly, what exactly is it metaphysically speaking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:05:46-07:00","id":1102121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102120#post1102120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malonkey said that you could make angels with prime and spirit. I think you could make something that, at a passing glance, look like an angel</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that is the point of the original idea - how to make a facsimile, not the real thing. Creating real ones would lead to a Fall, which treads too closely to template creation below archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:13:19-07:00","id":1102124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102121#post1102121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that is the point of the original idea - how to make a facsimile, not the real thing. Creating real ones would lead to a Fall, which treads too closely to template creation below archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that, but my point is larger: the fac-simile would lack most of the angels or demons powers. Most of them comes from a connection, past or present, to the God Machine. Much more than any other template, an angel takes its powers from its relationship with another being. You could probably make something that could try to register as an angel to supernatural powers but most of the powers of an angel could not be duplicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:24:39-07:00","id":1102125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102106#post1102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related - do we know what phase of Twilight Angels are in, as it relates to Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are in their own phase as written; so for Arcana, Prime is the most likley canditate for being able to see them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:51:22-07:00","id":1102147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102120#post1102120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since he wouldn't have a &quot;starting cover&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note, without a cover to shove all their &quot;self&quot; into, they wouldn't get a physical body to begin with. As far as I can tell, the false angel would fall from lack of infrastructure connecting it to the machine and then cease to exist because there is nowhere to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:55:08-07:00","id":1102148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102147#post1102147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, without a cover to shove all their &quot;self&quot; into, they wouldn't get a physical body to begin with. As far as I can tell, the false angel would fall from lack of infrastructure connecting it to the machine and then cease to exist because there is nowhere to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would rule he would &quot;materialize&quot; in Twilight. Like a demon with no more cover but with a spirit form instead of a physical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:57:20-07:00","id":1102150,"title":"","content":"Angels can exist without Cover as 'normal' ephemeral entities, so the lack of one isn't a large concern. Lack of connection to a God-Machine would be, but that's why we're creating Facsimiles and not trying to create the real thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:06:09-07:00","id":1102153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102148#post1102148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would rule he would &quot;materialize&quot; in Twilight. Like a demon with no more cover but with a spirit form instead of a physical one.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In the moment of the Fall, the angel\u2019s entire spiritual being is crammed into that body. Anything that doesn\u2019t fit is lost&quot;<br /> Based on this, the demonic form only actually exists because of the human body giving it a physical form to survive in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102150#post1102150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels can exist without Cover as 'normal' ephemeral entities, so the lack of one isn't a large concern. Lack of connection to a God-Machine would be, but that's why we're creating Facsimiles and not trying to create the real thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels can exist without Cover, I was responding to a mention of angels who fall without cover, where lack of one is a rather large concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 06-09-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:17:53-07:00","id":1102155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102153#post1102153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;In the moment of the Fall, the angel\u2019s entire spiritual being is crammed into that body. Anything that doesn\u2019t fit is lost&quot;<br /> Based on this, the spiritual form only actually exists because of the human body giving it a physical form to survive in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Angels can exist without Cover, I was responding to a mention of angels who fall without cover, where lack of one is a rather large concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but there's nothing to say that demons can't exist without physical form. I believe the destruction of anything that &quot;overspills&quot; is more about the limitation of the cover (which is the &quot;by default&quot; destination of a falling demon) than something inherent to demons. After all, there ARE demons without a cover, even if it happens long after the fall. IMHO, an angel without a cover who falls would simply end up in another state of being from your usual demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:22:47-07:00","id":1102156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102155#post1102155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, an angel without a cover who falls would simply end up in another state of being from your usual demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps being one of the Burned by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:54:04-07:00","id":1102161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102106#post1102106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related - do we know what phase of Twilight Angels are in, as it relates to Arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Demon is the one splat that is &quot;Sir Not Appearing In This Universe&quot; for me, I have always considered the GM to be the prime equivalent to Fallen Arcadia - the Fallen Aether, as it were. My replacement is the realm of subjective truth, with the prime-spirits being called Watchers. (Fate-twilight is filled with hedge beings that become immaterial and fuck with people's Fates. Draw on other kinds of faerie myths than the abduction kind.)<br /> <br /> So put angels in a Prime-twilight state <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Alternatively, every angel is aligned to one of the canon 3, whichever you prefer. Some spirits are death-aligned, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 06-09-2017, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T18:46:40-07:00","id":1102169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102124#post1102124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True that, but my point is larger: the fac-simile would lack most of the angels or demons powers. Most of them comes from a connection, past or present, to the God Machine. Much more than any other template, an angel takes its powers from its relationship with another being. You could probably make something that could try to register as an angel to supernatural powers but most of the powers of an angel could not be duplicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could make a facsimile of a Cover for it, with advanced Space, Fate and Time to give it the personal and temporal connections, and making it materialize and determining its appearance would be pretty basic magic all things considered. Come to think of it, you could probably bolster a Demon's Cover with Space, Time and Fate, too. Hm...<br /> <br /> If you were bound and determined, you could conceivably make something resembling an Angel, and give it something resembling a cover, but it would be a knockoff, and subject to Dissonance, because you don't have root access to reality like the GM does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T03:36:44-07:00","id":1102226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102169#post1102169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you could make a facsimile of a Cover for it, with advanced Space, Fate and Time to give it the personal and temporal connections, and making it materialize and determining its appearance would be pretty basic magic all things considered. Come to think of it, you could probably bolster a Demon's Cover with Space, Time and Fate, too. Hm...<br /> <br /> If you were bound and determined, you could conceivably make something resembling an Angel, and give it something resembling a cover, but it would be a knockoff, and subject to Dissonance, because you don't have root access to reality like the GM does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. For me an angelic cover, short of the very first dot, is way more extensive than anything you could do with supernal magic, short of archmastery. An angelic cover actually changes the universe on a large scale to accomodate the new being. It will create false pictures of him during that one trip to Tokyo in 78, modify his &quot;family&quot; memories in accordance, create memories in eyewitness at the time, change the records of the customs and of the airplane company, ... It's a change so complex on such a large scale, I don't see how you could do it with supernal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T04:44:47-07:00","id":1102233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1101798-granting-incepts-creating-false-angels?p=1102226#post1102226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. For me an angelic cover, short of the very first dot, is way more extensive than anything you could do with supernal magic, short of archmastery. An angelic cover actually changes the universe on a large scale to accomodate the new being. It will create false pictures of him during that one trip to Tokyo in 78, modify his &quot;family&quot; memories in accordance, create memories in eyewitness at the time, change the records of the customs and of the airplane company, ... It's a change so complex on such a large scale, I don't see how you could do it with supernal magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fully functional Cover in this way would probably fall under the Practice of Dynamics, therefore requiring archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}